# Scoped styles in Vue SFCs

Component styles belong in a **single** `<style scoped lang="scss">` block.

Do **not** add an unscoped `<style>` (even for select/modal/tooltip overlays).

If a ui-kit overlay teleports to `body` and scoped CSS cannot reach it:

1. Set **`:teleport="false"`** so the overlay stays in the component tree.
2. Style kit internals with **`:deep(...)`**.

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD: global styles from a Vue file -->
<ui-select popper-class="date-profile-select" />
<style lang="scss">
.date-profile-select.ui-select__popper { ... }
</style>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<ui-select :teleport="false" />
<style scoped lang="scss">
.field:deep(.ui-select__option) { ... }
</style>
```

App-wide tokens, resets, and ui-kit overrides stay in `apps/<app>/src/assets/scss/` (and `shared/assets/scss/`), not in SFCs.
